WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.580
Strata already brings field readings into
a satellite view.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.170
The headline and readings remain.

3
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.550
Moisture, vegetation, and canopy now share
one control.

4
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.510
Design Atlas supplies the references,

5
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.550
source evidence, and design tokens.

6
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.990
The direction is documented before it is
applied.

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.560
Choose moisture, vegetation, or canopy
temperature.

8
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.260
Open the reading context, then move
through the same four sections.

9
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.490
The original moisture, vegetation,

10
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.850
and temperature values stay intact.

11
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:42.590
A visible snapshot label keeps their
illustrative status in view.

12
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.260
The implementation includes reusable
components, brand tokens,

13
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.860
and the actual icon files, ready to carry
into a project.

14
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.680
This is still Strata.

15
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.620
Its field controls, tokens, and icons can
travel to the next page.
